461 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 248 0 R
/E ( We implemented activity logging in our system using PostgreSQL triggers and functions to automatically track changes in key tables like products and inventory_adjustments. A central function, log_activity\(\), handles logging for INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE actions. It records the table name, action type, user ID, timestamp, and details of modified columns. The user ID is fetched from a session variable \(myapp.user_id\), ensuring each action is linked to the user performing it.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
462 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 248 0 R
/E ( For inventory changes, we created a dedicated function, track_inventory_adjustments\(\), which logs stock additions and removals in the inventory_adjustments table. This function captures details like the product ID, quantity added or removed, and the user responsible for the adjustment. All activity is stored in the activity_logs table for auditing purposes.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
